WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.682
Your terminal programs

00:00:01.494 --> 00:00:02.401
can survive a

00:00:02.213 --> 00:00:03.038
restart

00:00:03.558 --> 00:00:04.784
Mitchell Hashimoto's

00:00:04.596 --> 00:00:05.727
Rex terminal can

00:00:05.539 --> 00:00:06.411
now resume your

00:00:06.223 --> 00:00:07.284
programs after a

00:00:07.096 --> 00:00:08.121
server restart

00:00:08.287 --> 00:00:09.194
and his company

00:00:09.006 --> 00:00:10.444
Superlogical published

00:00:10.256 --> 00:00:11.447
the protocol behind

00:00:11.258 --> 00:00:11.954
it today

00:00:12.478 --> 00:00:13.268
It's built on

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:13.881
a brand new

00:00:13.693 --> 00:00:15.166
open terminal protocol

00:00:15.308 --> 00:00:17.489
OSC 7577

00:00:17.726 --> 00:00:18.598
made with herdr

00:00:18.457 --> 00:00:19.364
and reviewed by

00:00:19.176 --> 00:00:20.909
several terminal emulator

00:00:20.721 --> 00:00:22.100
and program authors

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:23.742
Any program can

00:00:23.554 --> 00:00:24.367
report how to

00:00:24.179 --> 00:00:25.322
resume using plain

00:00:25.134 --> 00:00:26.324
escape sequences

00:00:26.466 --> 00:00:27.386
Rex ships with

00:00:27.197 --> 00:00:28.494
Claude Code support

00:00:28.542 --> 00:00:29.721
and herdr plans

00:00:29.532 --> 00:00:30.110
to add it

00:00:29.922 --> 00:00:30.558
next

00:00:31.086 --> 00:00:32.100
Full story on

00:00:31.911 --> 00:00:32.807
the dashboard
